{"Title":"An Act relative to the sales tax","BillNumber":"S1869","DocketNumber":"SD1347","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T15:57:06.963"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T15:57:06.9633333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1869/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Lewis, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1869) of Jason M. Lewis relative to the sales tax for certain purchases by rental companies.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tNotwithstanding the provisions of Section 8 of Chapter 64H of the General Laws or any general or special law or regulation to the contrary, including 830 CMR 64H,25,1(7), the purchase of a motor vehicle, trailer, or other vehicle by a rental company as so defined in section 32E ½ of chapter 175 of the general laws shall not be considered an exempt use from the sales tax at retail. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}